text:
Maya: quick check — running into a 403 when my service account JWT is exchanged for an access token in a multi-org setup. PR 5237 contains a small repro. The client ends up hitting the wrong project scope (fallback to the host project) and the token audience doesn't match the target service. anyone seen this pattern?
Samir: saw something like this last month. usually means the token exchange path is relying on implicit project scoping instead of an explicit `aud`/`target_audience`. can you paste the exchange snippet? :eyes:
Maya: here's the relevant bit from the node client config in the repro:```js
const opts = {
  clientEmail: process.env.SA_EMAIL,
  privateKey: process.env.SA_KEY,
  // we were relying on default project scoping here
  scope: ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform'],
};
await exchangeJwtForToken(opts);
```
Linh: yeah that will let the server pick the wrong project when there are nested org/folder bindings. try explicitly setting the audience and include the `project` claim in the JWT (or use `target_audience` param if your exchange endpoint supports it). e.g.:```js
const jwt = createJwt({
  iss: opts.clientEmail,
  sub: opts.clientEmail,
  aud: 'https://api.redwood.ai/',
  claims: { project: 'customer-project-123' }
});
await exchangeJwtForToken({ ...opts, jwt });
```
Samir: adding to that — if you're using the SDK's default token helper, there's an env var `RW_OVERRIDE_AUD` we added in staging to surface the audience override for this exact case. you can set it locally to confirm.
Maya: nice — set RW_OVERRIDE_AUD and the repro moved past the 403. thanks. quick follow up: PR 5237 has a failing integration test that proves the wrong-scope behavior. can someone from devex do a quick review + approve? cc @Alex
Alex: I'll take a look today. can you drop a brief checklist in the PR description of what to test locally (env vars, minimal steps)? i want to avoid flaky infra runs.
Maya: added steps in the PR description — two local env vars (SA_EMAIL, SA_KEY) + RW_OVERRIDE_AUD=test-aud. also included the recorded cassettes for the exchange call.
CI Bot: build/5237 — integration (linux) started · https://ci.redwood.ai/builds/5237 · status: queued
Alex: looked through the diff, small nit in error message wording but logic LGTM. left a tiny comment. will approve after CI is green. :thumbsup:
Samir: for the longer term we should add a validation step in the client that warns if `scope` only is used with multi-org setups and suggests `aud`/`target_audience`. low-priority ticket?
Linh: created ticket DEVEX-998 with repro details and suggested fixes (client validation + doc note). assigning to infra-auth for API-side support.
Maya: awesome — thanks team. once this merges i'll coordinate a quick note in the auth migration guide so infra teams don't hit this in prod. :raised_hands:
